                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "3db95512-e708-4b76-a1ac-09056c37a2cc",
                        "entry_id": "5b808534-1f33-3532-bf9e-3b72562f86a1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "суфражи́стках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "97343c57-9e3f-3ec9-8c32-432f9aac5368",
                        "entry_id": "5b808534-1f33-3532-bf9e-3b72562f86a1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "истор. сторонница и участница суфражизма, то есть движения за предоставление женщинам избирательных прав, распространенное во второй половине XIX века"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "56f8f17f-cc60-44c1-ac18-e72fcf46411e",
                                "sense_id": "97343c57-9e3f-3ec9-8c32-432f9aac5368",
                                "text": "Арестовано 121 суфражистка, в том числе их вождь г-жа Пангаерст, которая заявила, что демонстрация произведена с целью «обратить внимание общества на беспомощное положение женщин»."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "52070017-e3e7-4a27-84e7-aaf1fa75bfd8",
                                "sense_id": "97343c57-9e3f-3ec9-8c32-432f9aac5368",
                                "text": "Такие слова под стать какой-нибудь суфражистке. А я-то полагал, что вы ветреная Коломбина, игрушка в руках злого Арлекина."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8ca6f82b-9ebe-4288-8fec-cea45fd5dd67",
                        "source_entry_id": "5b808534-1f33-3532-bf9e-3b72562f86a1",
                        "source_sense_id": "97343c57-9e3f-3ec9-8c32-432f9aac5368",
                        "target_lang_word": "suffragist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "suffragist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "813462e2-ad02-3741-99dc-621c4d01161e",
                                        "entry_id": "3e8adf13-071b-3c56-a284-08985b8a6a58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who promotes suffrage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af52b54d-a8ab-44c2-8733-61f5d95245a7",
                                                "sense_id": "813462e2-ad02-3741-99dc-621c4d01161e",
                                                "text": "Other suffragists (like Susan B. Anthony and Alva Vanderbilt Belmont) and “suffragents” helped make the referendum a reality here. Ms. [Elaine] Weiss called New York “the linchpin” that put our country on the path to pass the 19th Amendment in 1920, granting women across the United States the right to vote."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e5a2b36-d9c0-3903-8c18-18de5795818e",
                                        "entry_id": "3e8adf13-071b-3c56-a284-08985b8a6a58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who votes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "suffragist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "64ce15db-f961-39ec-9674-17b086042700",
                                        "entry_id": "32e36c10-18a2-3e0e-98e4-96b6760df00a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, relating to, or promoting suffrage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c69d90d4-cec6-4511-a38c-e89f605c0cf7",
                                                "sense_id": "64ce15db-f961-39ec-9674-17b086042700",
                                                "text": "On June 4 the first speech was made by Senator [James Wolcott] Wadsworth [Jr.] of New York, whose very clever attack upon suffragist tactics was followed by an appeal to the economic fears and prejudices of his own prosperous class: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a3ae7bb-e612-4d8b-bbb4-45c062cfd78b",
                                                "sense_id": "64ce15db-f961-39ec-9674-17b086042700",
                                                "text": "She [Isabella Stewart Gardner] lived during one of the most tumultuous eras in American history, an era that included the Civil War, Reconstruction, the explosion of industrial capitalism and the rise of the socialist, trade-union, Populist, suffragist and transcendentalist movements."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad0f6332-06ba-4947-9a98-66add36fb986",
                                                "sense_id": "64ce15db-f961-39ec-9674-17b086042700",
                                                "text": "In examples that start from the nation’s earliest days — through suffragist movements, racial integration and the legalization of abortion — some of the biggest opponents of women’s rights have been women."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ae5e0812-079c-4836-9d01-3a5698b4afb7",
                        "source_entry_id": "5b808534-1f33-3532-bf9e-3b72562f86a1",
                        "source_sense_id": "97343c57-9e3f-3ec9-8c32-432f9aac5368",
                        "target_lang_word": "sufrażystka",
                        "target_lang_code": "pl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sufrażystka",
                                "target_lang_code": "pl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "718f8b17-eaee-35c1-b07d-902761c45cd7",
                                        "entry_id": "756bf46d-7ac9-3621-bf1e-d7ea5c2be04c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "działaczka walcząca o prawa wyborcze dla kobiet na przełomie XIX i XX wieku (głównie w krajach anglosaskich)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9fe0b1e2-6f31-46a3-8ae8-b68ceaedce52",
                                                "sense_id": "718f8b17-eaee-35c1-b07d-902761c45cd7",
                                                "text": "Po tym, jak angielska sufrażystka Emmeline Pankhurst poprowadziła marsz na parlament i wraz ze swoimi towarzyszkami stoczyła kilkugodzinną bitwę z policją, było wiadomo, że kobiety już nie ustąpią"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": [
